WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.560
It's kind of fall so today we will be reviewing the pumpkin spice latte.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:10.150
America's long tradition of combining sugar and artificial flavors.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:13.290
Oh, yea. Super orange.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.680
The aroma you really do get nutmeg.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.540
And I love nutmeg. It might be a prison drug, but I don't look down on it.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:27.550
I thin you could actually use this as a pumpkin spice creamer.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.240
In other coffee as well.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:35.040
You know if you let these guys sit for a while, grease kind of coagulates on top.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:39.880
It's kind of like a pumpkin spice lava lamp. I don't know if that's an advertise feature.

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:43.500
It's pretty good, I can see how you can kind of hooked on these.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:48.090
As far as coffee goes, that flavor is pretty much gone.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:52.200
We're just getting a lot of, a lot of good sugar and milk.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:55.340
Not that there's anything wrong with that... MMMM.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:01:04.770
This guy gets a good three stars. And it kind of leaves my tongue desperate for air.

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:06.460
or at least not sugar.

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:12.020
I could be bitter about this lack of coffee but that would be a silly expectation

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:16.850
This is it, they really jumped the shark here. Because as a pumpkin spice latte

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:23.380
but it's iced, if it was actually cold would I really want like a giant iced drink to cool off?

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:26.280
You know it doesn't quite, it doesn't quite make sense.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:30.140
You know these spice flavors are funny, it's like they're just almost there

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:31.590
but they're kind of missing something

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:37.390
A real spice might kind of get in your nose a little, it might kind of give you a tickling sensation.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:41.740
I think this one kind of cheats because it really improves as it waters down.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.130
You really can taste the coffee better in the iced one.

00:01:45.130 --> 00:01:51.890
Which I think is strangely ironic. So as long as you're comfortable being you know a post-modern individual

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.310
I think this is the winner, so we're giving it four stars.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:02:01.080
but you know the latte as we drink it the sort of build-your-own monstrosities that copies become

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.220
is totally like an American invention

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:12.680
an in that sense there's really nothing wrong with it. There's nothing that says that coffee needs to be this kind of European thing where it's always

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.330
always served in small glasses and things like that

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:20.890
You know, if people want... In America you can definitely do whatever you want.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:02:24.520
And that includes what coffee beverage you choose.

